    "title": "Upcoming Two-Week Closure of 13th Street NW for Water Main Project Begins October 23 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 hours ago The City of Great Falls, Montana, will close 13th Street NW between 3rd Avenue NW and 1st Avenue NW starting October 23, 2025. The closure is for a water main replacement project that began earlier this month and will continue through November.\nCentral Plumbing, Heating, Excavation is the contractor for the project. Detour signs will direct drivers. Access to homes, schools, and businesses will be maintained during the two-week closure. Residents can contact Senior Civil Engineer Matt Proud or contractor representative Kris Liggett for more information.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
